.TH HSH 1
.SH NAME
hsh \- simple_shell - a Unix command line interpreter.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ./hsh
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B hsh
is a customised Unix command line interpreter that executes commands read, emulating basic features of the POSIX standard unix shell. It prints a prompt, reads an input, parses the arguments into tokens, searches the environment path and executes commands in an independant forked child process.
.PP
The application supports interactive terminal interaction, signals like Ctrl+C are successfully caught to keep the shell session running.

.SH FEATURES
The shell supports absolute and relative path executions.
.TP
.B exit
Terminates the shell, the execution exits back to the parent process using the return code of the most recent command pipeline.
.TP
.B env
Prints all global environment key\-value pairs associated with the active terminal profile to stdout.

.SH ERROR HANDLING
If a command cannot be resolved within the environment paths, \fBhsh\fR writes a descriptive diagnostic error trace directly into standard error formatting:
.IP
\fI./hsh: 1: <command>: not found\fR
.PP
Internal engine operations automatically free allocated heap structures during unexpected fork failures, execution faults, or EOF terminations to preserve memory sanitization boundaries.

